  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DP - Emergency Response and Assistance to Displaced Populations in Niger</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Niger is one of the least developed countries in the world, with one of the poorest socio-economic and development indicators and the highest demographic growth. As reported in the Humanitarian Needs Overview (HNO) 2022 and Humanitarian Response Plan (HRP) 2022, Niger continues to face acute and complex humanitarian crises marked by the impact of various shocks. This project aims to deliver humanitarian assistance to improve the living conditions, resilience, dignity, and protection of crisis affected populations in Diffa, Maradi, Tahoua, and Tillab&#xE9;ry, which are four conflict-affected regions in Niger. The intervention aims to provide emergency shelters, transitional shelters, non-food items kits, and needs-based protection-specific kits including hygiene kits inclusive of menstrual hygiene management items, baby kits, and education kits. The intervention is also preventing, mitigating and responding to protection risks such as gender-based violence and trafficking in persons, while reinforcing the capacities of field practitioners and community members to anticipate, identify and address those risks. In addition, the project is promoting the mobilization and empowerment of communities, as well as strengthening access to protection assistance, mental health and psychosocial support, education, and water, sanitation and hygiene services.</narrative>
  </description>
